  "final_message": "The root cause was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`. Its filter was `status == \"open\" or (next_attempt_at is not None and next_attempt_at <= now)`. Because of operator precedence, every open invoice counted as due on every billing run, whatever its retry schedule said. The filter now requires all three conditions: the invoice is open, it has a `next_attempt_at`, and that time has arrived.\n\nThe 24 existing tests pass, but I didn't add a test for this case, and I didn't run a scenario that checks the 4-attempts-in-a-week behavior directly. `answer.json` is written at the repo root with `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.",
